$meta
  title = Maid Aura Café
  description = Inherit a maid café staffed by Pokémon employees. Manage, train, and build relationships.
  tags = rpg, cafe, management, simulation, pokemon

customerComments
  "The coffee here is absolutely divine!"
  "That Lucario in the maid dress made my whole morning."
  "Cutest café staff I've ever seen, no contest."
  "The pastries literally melt in your mouth."
  "Service was a bit slow today but the staff is adorable."
  "I came for the coffee and stayed for the view."
  "Best café in the district, hands down."
  "The little Riolu almost dropped my order but he was so earnest. Left a big tip."
  "I've never seen such dedicated employees. Whatever they're paying them, it's not enough."
  "The atmosphere here is... charged. In a good way."

dayDescriptions
  The morning sun filters through the café windows, casting warm light across the polished counters.
  A gentle breeze carries the scent of fresh coffee beans through the propped-open door.
  The café awakens to the rhythmic sound of grinding beans and clinking ceramic.
  Rain patters against the windows — a cozy day that draws hot drink lovers in droves.
  The morning rush begins as the first customers line up outside, breath visible in the cool air.
  Golden afternoon light floods the seating area, making everything glow amber and honey.
  The smell of fresh baking drifts out onto the street, pulling in passersby.

eveningDescriptions
  The last customers drain their cups and head out into the night. You flip the sign to "Closed" and begin wiping down the counters.
  Chairs are stacked on tables, the floors are swept, and the kitchen falls quiet. The café exhales after a long day.
  The neon "OPEN" sign flickers off. You count the register in the silence, the only sound the hum of the refrigerator.
  The final pot of coffee goes cold on the burner as you lock the front door. Tomorrow it starts all over again.
  You take out the trash, the alley dark and cool. Back inside, the café feels different empty — smaller, somehow.
  The last employee hangs up their apron. You're alone with the ledger, the receipts, and the quiet ticking of the wall clock.
  Lights dim, the espresso machine powers down with a weary hiss. You do a final walk-through, checking locks and leaving nothing for tomorrow.
  The mop bucket water turns grey as you finish the floors. You flip off the lights, the café dark and still, ready for tomorrow.
